  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Yemen Economic Stabilisation Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">he Yemen Economic Stabilisation (YES) Programme strengthens the Government of Yemen&#x2019;s (GoY) capability to deliver essential, inclusive services by addressing core drivers of economic instability through targeted, politically informed technical assistance. Through a politically oriented and conflict sensitive approach, YES supports reforms in public financial management, monetary stability, electricity sector, and the financial sector, while creating conditions for private-sector investment and job creation. By stabilising essential GoY economic governance, the programme over time enhances the government&#x2019;s credibility and legitimacy, maintaining a pathway to a political process, and reduces humanitarian needs. Beneficiaries include Yemeni citizens (particularly in GoY-controlled areas) and vulnerable households, as well as core economic institutions such as the Central Bank, Ministry of Finance, and energy authorities.</narrative>
  </description>
